Z||000012||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||11:03 PM||||yeah i had wheel hop through 330' mark.. we video taped a few runs and 3 out of 4 i had wheel hop the 4th.. i wasn't running nitrous! we fixed the wheel hop with a passenger and a 80# bag of quikcrete in the trunk! it was only a 40 HP shot but with the fuel i had and the right amoung of nitrous it was 130lbft (yeah at the wheels) i used the 40hp 80lbft one for the street. <P>Jeff i can keep up with SIs i used to be able to wax the floor with them!!  I need MORE GO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but i'm MUCH prettier than they are! LAME blue cars!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Lowfunds.. A520s ROCK!!!! get em if ya can!!! you'll love them! I did!  my W-10s are nice and stickey too.. i couldn't wait the 7  dyas for the Yoko delivery.. i didn't have tires/wheels at all! so i opted for the dunlops and i got a killer deal on them! $411.17 m/b/road hazzard! no my plate will soon say  NUKKEN  if you know Dutch you'll understand..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Eric Marsh||11-11-2000||10:58 AM||||Don't know about your '87, but on my '88 I went to a 225 on a 17"x7" wheel with a 45mm offset up front and a 245 on an 18"x8" with a 40 offset on the rear. I would have preferred a 50 offset up front as those wheels stick out a very small amount more than the rear, but you can't really tell by looking at the car. Here is a picture of my Fiero with those wheels on:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hotrodder.com/emarsh/images/new_wheels.JPG"> ||||reg||1
